  "strategy": "Create a multi-strategy optimization algorithm that minimizes the convolution peak with respect to the sequence sum. The algorithm operates in three main phases:\n\n1. Genetic Algorithm Initialization:\n   - Start with the parent sequence if available, otherwise create a uniform sequence of length 1000\n   - Generate 49 additional initial candidates using different distributions:\n        \u2022 1 triangular (peak in middle)\n        \u2022 1 linear ramp (increasing then mirrored decreasing)\n        \u2022 5 sinusoidal variations with increasing damping factor\n        \u2022 3 bimodal Gaussian distributions (50k/total, 100k/total, 150k/total)\n        \u2022 6 random initialization attempts\n        \u2022 9 side-biased distributions (3 left, 3 right, 3 full)\n\n2. Optimization:\n   - For each candidate, normalize to ensure sum >=0.01 and clip to [0,1000]\n   - Use a min-peak LP solver to maximize the sequence sum while keeping the convolution max bounded\n   - Try aggressive perturbations up to 3% but always check for better results via reconvolution\n   - Implement multiple repair strategies including:\n        \u2022 Uniform perturbation to a random length from 950-1050\n        \u2022 Linear crossover between sequences\n        \u2022 Subgradient momentum with weighted restarts\n   - Schedule:\n        \u2022 Evaluate candidates and update the best\n        \u2022 For each candidate, perform up to 800 evaluations through various iterative methods\n        \u2022 Use time budgeting: 1200s for LP-related methods, 300s for perturbation\n\n3. Phase 5 Handling:\n   - Final polishing with cross-validation between all previously used methods\n   - Create a mix of interpolation methods (linear, gaussian, sinc) to explore diverse shapes\n   - Apply the kill-switch: if the objective doesn't improve for 100 consecutive evaluations, terminate",
